{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544454-aa-legacy-for-council-of-dragons","id":1544454,"title":"[AA] Legacy for Council of Dragons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-22T04:44:00-07:00","id":1544454,"title":"[AA] Legacy for Council of Dragons","content":"Is there <b>Legacy </b>- fan or official - for members of <b>Adamantine Arrows Council of Dragons faction? </b>Some AA strategist, probably based on Mind or Time, i suppose? I cannot find one on <a href=\"https://codexofdarkness.com/wiki/Legacies_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">CoD Codex page</a>.<br /> <br /> Short sum-up of Council of Dragons faction from Tome of Pentacle:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Philosopher-strategists, the Council of Dragons believe that while warriors must achieve physical skill to serve the Arrow and be well-rounded humans, the deepest well of martial skill is found in the mind. Councilors devote themselves to the metaphysics of conflict, and the eternal patterns of strategy, manifested through numerous battlefields and technologies. The depth of such studies is such that no Arrow can master them all. Thus, the Council encourages specialization despite the Order\u2019s broader bias against such things. In any emergency, the senior Councilor is the one with the greatest applicable knowledge: something bound to change when the nucleus of conflict moves from chemical warfare to enchanted Bronze Age swords.<br /> <br /> One goal of the faction is to find the \u201cSecond Wisdom,\u201d which is the ability to understand the unbiased truth about a situation, and find a path between what is absolutely moral, versus what is tactically optimal. The search produces a broad spread of opinions, leading to reputations ranging from bloodthirst to excessive idealism on the part of individual Councilors. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T10:42:38-07:00","id":1544473,"title":"","content":"While the Awakening Gambit are probably best suited for the Alethian faction, they're arguably also a great fit in the Council of Dragons. They're focused on Mind and Time, and their abilities require and involve quite a lot of strategy. Other Legacies aren't as much of an intuitive fit for the Council of Dragons, but I feel you can fairly justifiably use a Time Legacy like the House of Ariadne, Stewards of the Celestial Orrey, or the Eleventh Question. You could also probably make a case for a Subtle One whose focus is patterns of conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T10:47:16-07:00","id":1544475,"title":"","content":"The first Legacy I ever wrote, the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\"><i>Agathos Kai Sophos </i></a>(Mind/Time), were made to be enlightened strategists for the Council of Dragons. <br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1057333#post1057333\"><i>Awakening Gambit </i></a>(Mind/Time) might also work, turning their strategic accumen to optimize the battles of the Awakened.<br /> <br /> The members of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1109045#post1109045\"><i>Cloud Infinite </i></a>(Mind/Prime)would also make for brilliant strategists, provided they were discrete enough or the situation desperate enough to require their help.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the <i>Aurora Auricalcinae</i> (Time/Space), a Legacy of hermetic diviners mentioned on page 81 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>, might also qualify, but you would need to flesh them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{